SUMMARY:Pet Portrait Collage with Li Newton
DESCRIPTION:Goals:\n-Have fun.\n-Learn basic analog (cut by hand) paper collage techniques.\n-Learn how to transfer a photo onto a surface.\n-Basic cutting and gluing\, building layers to create depth.\n-Complete the foundation of building a portrait of your favorite fur or feathered friend. \nMaterials Provided:\n-Practice boards and panels will be provided.\n-I will also provide a wide selection of papers and gel medium\, some scissors\, paper towels\, finger cots. \nYou will bring:\n– 8 X 10 photo of your pet — PRINTED on paper. This is a PORTRAIT class so please have head of pet fill much of the page rather than a full photo of your animal or tiny animal running in a landscape.\n– Extra colorful papers\, magazines\, etc.\, that have a variety of colors and textures.\n– Apron or clothes you do mind getting a little glue on. \nDon’t forget to bring a beverage and snack. \nThis can be a serious portrait or something whimsical and silly. If you think you “can’t draw”\, I’ll teach you a way to “cheat” to get the image down. \nEveryone can do this! Don’t be intimidated. It’s all about learning\, experimenting\, community and having fun!\nRegister at https://www.tracksidestudios.com
URL:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/pet-portrait-collage-with-li-newton-2/
LOCATION:Trackside Studios\, 375 Depot Street\, Asheville\, 28801
CATEGORIES:Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Hazel_Pet-Portrait-Class.jpg
GEO:35.5805429;-82.5646109
