SUMMARY:Spring Botanicals in Watercolors with local artist Casi Fordham
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the arrival of Spring with creativity\, community & fresh flowers at your table! \nIn this class you will learn the foundational techniques in watercolor painting\, using fresh Spring blooms as your inspiration. We will have plenty of blooms available for you\, and if you have some blooms from your garden or elsewhere that you love\, feel free to bring some along! \nLocal watercolor artist Casi Fordham will guide you in learning various wet into wet watercolor techniques\, dry-brushing & using dark & light values as you build layers of color and shape to create your blooms\, adding details and embellishments afterward. \nAllowing the pigment and water to interact as they expand across the page together is a great way to trust the creative process as it unfolds. Watercolors have a way of leading and surprising you if you allow them to! \nYou will begin with a step-by-step watercolor demo where you will warm-up with Casi’s guidance\, and then transition into several rounds of layering and painting on your background papers. We’ll explore basic techniques\, break down the elements of building values\, guided by demos each step along the way. You will bring home your practice pieces as well as a larger piece you’ll work up to. \nPLEASE BRING WITH YOU: a vase for your flower (s) that you will place in front of you for visual reference. \nA light afternoon snack and a glass of wine will be served. \nAll materials provided. No experience needed. \nCome play\, learn & create!
URL:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/watercolor-botanicals-with-casi-fordham-2/
LOCATION:ArtPlay Studio\, 53 Orange Street\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801
CATEGORIES:Classes,Events
